 ],
 "answer_text": "Found 11 disease records and 2 gene records for BRCA1 and BRCA2 [1][2][3][4][6][7][8][9][10][11][12][13][14]. \n\nBRCA1-Associated Diseases\n\nBRCA1 is linked to familial cancer of breast [1], familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1 [2], pancreatic cancer susceptibility 4 [3], and Fanconi anemia complementation group S [4]. The gene encodes a nuclear phosphoprotein that acts as a tumor suppressor, combining with other tumor suppressors and DNA damage sensors to form the BRCA1-associated genome surveillance complex (BASC) [5]. Mutations in BRCA1 are responsible for approximately 40% of inherited breast cancers and more than 80% of inherited breast and ovarian cancers [5]. \n\nBRCA2 is associated with medulloblastoma [6], Fanconi anemia complementation group D1 [7], familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 2 [8], glioma susceptibility 3 [9], familial prostate cancer [10], pancreatic cancer susceptibility 2 [11], and Wilms tumor 1 [12]. \n\nGene records found\n\nGene NCBIGene:672, name: BRCA1 DNA repair associated [13]. Gene NCBIGene:675, name: BRCA2 DNA repair associated [14]. Gene symbol: BRCA1 [15]. \n\nDisease records found\n\nDisease name: Familial cancer of breast [1]. Disease name: Familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 1 [2]. Disease name: Pancreatic cancer susceptibility 4 [3]. Disease name: Fanconi anemia complementation group S [4]. Disease name: Medulloblastoma [6]. Disease name: Fanconi anemia complementation group D1 [7]. Disease name: Familial breast-ovarian cancer susceptibility 2 [8]. Disease name: Glioma susceptibility 3 [9]. Disease name: Familial prostate cancer [10]. Disease name: Pancreatic cancer susceptibility 2 [11]. Disease name: Wilms tumor 1 [12]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: BRCA1: An Endocrine and Metabolic Regulator [16]. Pubmed title: Preneoplastic stromal cells promote BRCA1-mediated breast tumorigenesis [20]. Pubmed title: Mechanism of BRCA1-BARD1 function in DNA end resection and DNA protection [23]. Pubmed title: Targeting GPX4-mediated ferroptosis protection sensitizes BRCA1-deficient cancer cells to PARP inhibitors [26]. Pubmed title: BRCA1 Promoter Methylation in Ovarian Cancer: Clinical Relevance and a Novel Diagnostic Approach Using Fragment Analysis [29]. \n\nClinvar records found\n\nClinvar title: NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.5243_5277+2788del [17]. Clinvar title: NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.5277+2916_5277+2946delinsGG [21]. Clinvar title: NG_005905.2:g.(147057_150288)_(160933_166866)del [24]. Clinvar title: GRCh37/hg19 17q21.31(chr17:41267743-41267796)x3 [27]. Clinvar title: NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.2145C>G (p.Thr715=) [30]. \n\nOmim records found\n\nBRCA1 DNA REPAIR-ASSOCIATED PROTEIN [18]. BRCA1 [18]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: Germline BRCA1 and BRCA2 Mutations in Jewish Women Affected by Breast Cancer [19]. Clinical trial name: BRCA1 Haploinsufficiency and Gene Expression [22]. Clinical trial name: Study to Evaluate Treatment Customized According to RAP80 and BRCA1 in Patients With Advanced Lung Carcinoma [25]. Clinical trial name: Letrozole in Preventing Breast Cancer in Postmenopausal Women With a BRCA1 or BRCA2 Mutation [28]. Clinical trial name: Recombinant Human Chorionic Gonadotropin in Preventing Breast Cancer in Premenopausal Women With BRCA1 Mutations [31]. "
